; Tutorial_8_Read_the_Results.inix -- a spoken walk through BatCon, written for buildTutorials (the format is
; described at the top of Tutorial_0_Overview.inix in the Homer kit's Templates).

[about]
Title=8 - Read the Results
Intro=The results window, the log, and what a failure says.
Setup=BatCon has just finished a batch.
Homework=After a batch, read its results and open its log.

[step]
Say=When a batch ends, a window lists every file: converted, skipped or failed.
Hear=BatCon results

[step]
Say=The first line is the summary. Down Arrow reads each file in turn.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Failed Notes dot p d f: the conversion made an empty file

[step]
Say=A failure says why. The last line names the log, which has every detail, one file for each run.
Key=Control+End
Hear=The log: C:\Users\you\AppData\Local\BatCon\logs\BatCon-20261019-120000.log

[step]
Say=Escape closes the window, and the reader says nothing more until you move.
Key=Escape
Note=The reader says nothing as the window closes.

[step]
Say=What this walk taught: the summary first, a reason for each failure, and the log at the end.
